# tmux-control — user configuration
# Sourced by every script in bin/. Edit this file to adapt the skill to your
# project. Environment variable TMUX_CONTROL_PROTECTED_RE overrides PROTECTED_RE.

# PROTECTED_RE — ERE matched against process command lines. Processes matching
# this pattern are considered "long-running / important":
#   - tmux-kill-pane refuses to kill panes containing them (unless --force)
#   - check-tmux-destructive lists them in warnings before kill-session etc.
#   - tmux-status --procs shows them (together with any python process)
# Keep this project-specific; the defaults below cover common long-running jobs.
PROTECTED_RE='train\.py|trainer|scheduler|monitor|jupyter|serve|uvicorn|gunicorn|celery|streamlit|worker|daemon'

# PROCS_RE — pattern used by `tmux-status --procs` when listing processes.
PROCS_RE="python|node|$PROTECTED_RE"

# EXTRA_DESTRUCTIVE_RE (optional) — additional command patterns that
# check-tmux-destructive should treat as destructive, e.g. your project's
# whole-session stop script:
# EXTRA_DESTRUCTIVE_RE='myscript\.py\s+--stop\b'
EXTRA_DESTRUCTIVE_RE="${EXTRA_DESTRUCTIVE_RE:-}"
